<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining lowers indium price by 5,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining lowers indium price by 5,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said on Tuesday it would lower its indium price by 5,000 yen per kg to 30,000 yen per kg for large lots and 35,000 yen for small lots, effective from Wednesday shipments.</p>
<p>The price cut was in reaction to movements in overseas markets, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company last announced a price change on July 19, when it lowered the price by 5,000 yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
